DAW Pro local patch 0004 against signalsmith-stretch v1.3.2 (57b93f4e9206a089a45387eaa39bdc9f310d3308) + patches 0001, 0002, 0003

Formant envelope through the harmonic peaks, when the caller gives the
fundamental (setFormantBase(f), f > 0).

With formant compensation on, updateFormants() builds each block's spectral
envelope by spreading every band's energy outwards with a per-band decay of
1 - 1/(f/2 + 1) (f = the harmonic spacing in bands), then shrinking it back
with the inverse. Over one spacing the spread falls about e^-2 (-8.7 dB), so
between two strong harmonics the envelope sags about 4.3 dB, and a harmonic
more than about 8.7 dB below a neighbour reads the neighbour's skirt instead
of its own level. The shrink pass is a no-op on a spread array (measured:
deleting it changes the output by float rounding only). The compensation
divides the target envelope by this one, so the output harmonics land off
the input's envelope: at 220 Hz -5 st up to +6.3/-7.1 dB (RMS 3.02 dB over
250-2500 Hz, upstream's own API). With the input's TRUE envelope substituted
for the estimate and nothing else changed: 0.06 dB. The estimate is the
error, not the compensation arithmetic. In DAW Pro this was natural tuning's
c = 1 over-correction on down-shifts (220 Hz -5 st read +63.2 c against a
50 c bound).

The patch replaces both passes, when a base is set and the spacing is above
1.5 bands, with an envelope through the harmonic peaks. A band is a peak when
no strictly larger band lies within half a harmonic spacing on either side,
and it is strictly larger than its left neighbour. Consecutive peaks are
joined by straight lines in log energy, and the outermost peaks are held
outwards. freqToBand() subtracts half a band, so the spacing is
freqEstimate + 0.5 bands. The nearest strictly larger band on each side
comes from a monotonic stack, so the pass is O(bands) for any base. The
buffers are sized in configure(), and nothing is allocated per block.

WITH NO BASE, UPSTREAM'S CODE RUNS UNCHANGED (css_set_formant_preserve, the
clip flag). Upstream's own estimate returns 0 or a multiple of f0 on steady
vowels (147 Hz: twice the spacing; 196, 294, 330, 440 Hz: 0). The new
envelope needs the true spacing: with an octave-high estimate it joins only
every other harmonic.

Measured (DAW Pro's render loop and meters, ported and matched line for line
against a real NT-E1 test log; 72 cells, 110-440 Hz x +-100..700 c, c = 1):
- per-harmonic level error vs the ideal (RMS, 250-2500 Hz): 3.94 -> 2.63 dB
  mean, better in 63/72 cells, worse by > 1 dB in none;
- the cepstral envelope meter: 51 -> 69 of 72 cells within +-50 c;
  220 Hz -5 st 63.2 -> 16.5 c;
- 2.5-5 kHz (partials 55-85 dB below the strongest; the render floor
  dominates): 5.49 -> 4.39 dB mean, worse by > 1 dB in 6/72 cells;
- byte-identical to 0001-0003: every render with no base (flag on: 36/36
  dumped cells, and every flag-on value of the 72-cell map), the formant
  stage withheld (36/36), and an engaged render at 0 st (6/6 f0 from 80 to 440 Hz; -1 c differs).
  NOT byte-identical: c = 0 (an engaged amount whose formant curve follows
  the pitch) differs at float rounding, max 2.2e-6 (<= -111 dB re peak, 7
  cells); it is engaged, so formantRenderVersion re-keys it anyway;
- hostile input (silence, a 1e-20 signal, a sine, noise, an impulse, a
  full-scale square; bases 0.5x/2x/50 Hz/20 kHz): no NaN, Inf or subnormal
  output, and silence stays silence;
- a wrong base: 1.5x reads as 1x; 0.75x holds on average but 330 Hz
  degrades; 0.5x and 2x break it (2x breaks upstream too). A window of 0.6
  spacings (not shipped) holds at 0.75x as well, but was not measured on
  sung vibrato;
- cost: an engaged render got CHEAPER: -6.7 % CPU at -O2 (-1.4 % at the test
  build's -O0); the formant stage alone -23 %. Medians of 9 interleaved
  pairs of 60 s renders, clock() CPU time, under timing.lock with both heavy
  slots free (load average 8-10 from other work); at -O2 no patched sample
  was slower than any shipped one (at -O0 the ranges overlap);
THIS PATCH CHANGES THE BYTES OF EVERY RENDER WITH AN EXPLICIT FORMANT BASE
(every engaged natural-tuning render): the render cache must re-key them
(PitchEditSet.formantRenderVersion 2 -> 3, digest slot 7). Renders with no
base keep their bytes and their keys.

Filed upstream: not yet (draft report ready; like #31-#33, only on the
user's word).

